   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1045937">This instruction converts the low FP64 value in the second source operand to an FP16 value, and stores the result in the low element of the destination operand.</para>
  <para unique="1045938">When the conversion is inexact, the value returned is rounded according to the rounding control bits in the MXCSR register.</para>
  <para unique="1045939">Bits 127:16 of the destination operand are copied from the corresponding bits of the first source operand. Bits MAXVL-1:128 of the destination operand are zeroed. The low FP16 element of the destination is updated according to the writemask.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1045941">VCVTSD2SH dest, src1, src2 </title>
   <programlisting>IF *SRC2 is a register* and (EVEX.b = 1):
	SET_RM(EVEX.RC)
ELSE:
	SET_RM(MXCSR.RC)
IF k1[0] OR *no writemask*:
	DEST.fp16[0] := Convert_fp64_to_fp16(SRC2.fp64[0])
ELSE IF *zeroing*:
	DEST.fp16[0] := 0
// else dest.fp16[0] remains unchanged
DEST[127:16] := SRC1[127:16]
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_cvt_roundsd_sh (__m128h a, __m128d b, const int rounding);
VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_mask_cvt_roundsd_sh (__m128h src, __mmask8 k, __m128h a, __m128d b, const int rounding);
VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_maskz_cvt_roundsd_sh (__mmask8 k, __m128h a, __m128d b, const int rounding);
VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_cvtsd_sh (__m128h a, __m128d b);
VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_mask_cvtsd_sh (__m128h src, __mmask8 k, __m128h a, __m128d b);
VCVTSD2SH __m128h _mm_maskz_cvtsd_sh (__mmask8 k, __m128h a, __m128d b);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1045963">Invalid, Underflow, Overflow, Precision, Denormal.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1045968" format="xIndent1">EVEX-encoded instructions, see <link unique="1045966" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#63155: 06_Table: Table 2-47. Type E3 Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page with period">Table&#160;2&#8209;49, &#8220;Type E3 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
